2025-10-08 12:26:36,973 [WARNING] Skipped idx=816: gold or llm supporting sentence is empty. gold='', llm='In the context, it is mentioned that TAp73 regulates the spindle assembly checkpoint by modulating BubR1 activity. The role of various p73 isoforms in tumorigenesis has been controversial, but recent studies have shown that TAp73-deficient (TAp73(-/-)) mice reveal the tumor-suppressive functions of TAp73 isoforms. This suggests an emerging role for Trp-73 in maintaining genomic stability. Additionally, TAp73(-/-) mice are infertile and produce oocytes with spindle abnormalities, indicating a link between TAp73 activities and the molecular machinery underlying meiosis and mitosis. The spindle assembly checkpoint (SAC) complex, which includes Bub1, Bub3, and BubR1, is involved in regulating these processes. TAp73 interacts directly with these SAC components and is involved in their localization and activities. Furthermore, decreased TAp73 expression correlates with increased SAC protein expression in lung cancer patients, establishing TAp73 as a regulator of SAC responses and indicating that TAp73 loss can lead to mitotic arrest defects. These findings support the importance of TAp73 in maintaining genomic stability and preventing tumors through its regulation of the SAC complex.'
